      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SOHO PIASTRI (1) had enough speed to lead from a wide barrier and win easily two back at this circuit and distance before a midfield finish in a stronger line-up last time. This suits better and he should get his chance from the ace draw. Stablemate SOHO WASHINGTON (4) returns to the city in fine form having put three wins together at Penrith. He looks up to a race like this so could extend the winning streak. PURE GRUNT (2) is back in winning form having led throughout at Newcastle last time. Can take advantage of a low draw and owns a good record at the mile. LEWIE KELLY (3) steps up in grade but is in fine form, putting two wins together at Newcastle. Led in both of those so can push forward from a favourable draw. LOCHINVAR MARCELLO (8) draws wide but his consistency is hard to knock having assembles a string of wins and placings.",
